# No Guessing

Never guess in the process of doing anything. When a fact is unknown —
a file's contents, a value, a selector, a class name, how a shared
module behaves, where something lives, or what the user intends — you
must **verify it**, not assume it. Guessing is a non-negotiable
violation of how work is done in this app.

## What counts as guessing (banned)

- Inventing file paths, class names, selectors, function names, or
  values instead of reading them from the actual source.
- Assuming how a shared module behaves (`js/marketing-shell.js`,
  `js/agent-menu.js`, `js/topbar.js`, `js/count-up-all.js`, etc.)
  without opening it.
- Copying nav/shell/module structure "from memory" instead of from the
  canonical source (`pages/wiseai.html`).
- Reporting a visual change as done without actually verifying it
  (see the `visual-verify` skill), in both light and dark mode.
- Filling ambiguity in the user's request with an assumption when the
  answer materially changes the outcome.

## Rules for the agent

- **Verify before you act.** Read the relevant file, run the search, or
  check the canonical page before making a change that depends on it.
- If you cannot verify something and it materially affects the result,
  **ask the user** rather than proceeding on a guess.
- Prefer sensible, stated defaults only for trivial choices (naming,
  formatting) — never for facts you can look up.
- If you are unsure whether something is true, say so explicitly and
  confirm it before relying on it. Do not present an assumption as fact.
